# Numbers, units, measures and names with special characters.
The field "floors" is at least 2.
The field "floors" is at most 30.
The field "capacity" is greater than 0.5.
The field "épsilon" is less than 0.00001.
The field "large" is at most 1234567.
The field "huge" is at most 10000000000000000.
The field "integer" is at least 007.
The field "tab	name" is at least 1.25.
The field "bar\name" is at least 100000.
The clock "clock" has the unit "s".
The value "speed" has the unit "s".
The value "rate" has the unit "Hz".
The value "duration" has the unit "parsecs".
The value "door_time" is mutable.
The module "m" has the unit "ms".
The module "m" reads the value "rate".
The value "x" has the same unit as the value "y".
The value "y" has the same unit as the value "x".
The value "z" has the unit "s".
The module "n" has the unit "s".
The module "n" uses the value "x".
The module "n" consumes the value "w".
The value "w" has the same unit as the value "rate".
The queue "queue" is bounded.
The queue "q2" is closed.
The state machine "sm" has the states "a", "b" and "c".
The state machine "sm" starts in the state "a".
The module "m" moves the state machine "sm" from the state "a" to the state "b".
If the queue "q2" is full, the module "m" always drops the message "x" from the queue "q2".
When the module "m" reads the value "rate" and the value "z", the module "m" never changes the value "z".
The module "m" does not mutate.
The module "m" never writes "x" to the file "f".
